+    <Warning>
+      Direct upload accepts files up to **200 MiB**. The file is passed to the worker
+      inside the task queue message, so the API, Redis and the worker each hold a copy
+      of it in memory. An Apple Health export from a few years of Apple Watch use is
+      usually larger, so use the multipart upload for real exports. If
+      `APPLE_XML_MAX_FILE_SIZE_BYTES` is set lower, that limit applies here too.
+    </Warning>
+
+    | Status | Meaning |
+    |--------|---------|
+    | `200 OK` | File queued for processing |
+    | `401` | Invalid or missing API key |
+    | `413` | File is over 200 MiB. Use the multipart upload |
+    | `422` | The request has no `file` part |
+    | `503` | The task queue is unavailable. Retry with backoff |
+
+    <ResponseExample>
+    ```json 413 File too large
+    {
+      "title": "Content Too Large",
+      "status": 413,
